 "section_summary": "This section contains the concluding part of the American Embassy in Tokyo's monthly report for July 1938 (along with its registers of despatches and telegrams sent) and the opening portion of Despatch No. 3265 transmitting the monthly report for August 1938. The documents highlight serious diplomatic friction between the United States and Japan over assaults on American citizens, aerial bombings of mission properties in China, the shooting down of a commercial CNAC passenger airliner, and restrictions on U.S. naval navigation on the Yangtze River. The reports also record Japanese military operations advancing on Hankow, severe Soviet-Japanese border clashes and a subsequent truce at Changkufeng, strained Anglo-Japanese relations, and growing Japanese political centralization and wartime economic mobilization.",
